  "title": "De revolutionibus orbium coelestium (Copernicus, 1543)",
  "summary": "Copernicus's De revolutionibus was printed in Nuremberg in 1543 by Johannes Petreius, with Rheticus supervising the printing. The book aimed to restore uniform circular motion to the planetary theory of Ptolemy's Almagest, and its heliostatic claims placed the Sun at the centre. An anonymous preface by Osiander presented them as a hypothesis.",
